# Copy to .env and fill in for real bot replies. Without OPENROUTER_API_KEY
# the bot uses canned mock replies so the game still runs end to end locally.
PORT=8787
DB_PATH=./botcha.sqlite
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Enables /api/bot-test/reply and the /#/bot-test page. Local dev only: the
# endpoint has no auth and no rate limit, so exposing it hands the internet a
# free LLM proxy billed to the key above.
BOT_TEST=

# Paid model, chosen by benchmarking candidates against the real persona
# prompt (SPEC 5) on English AND Persian tables — players do not all chat in
# English, and a bot that answers an all-Persian table in English is an
# instant tell. Roughly $0.22 per 1000 games at ~600 prompt + 40 completion
# tokens x 3 bot turns, so cost is not the deciding factor; behaviour is.
#
# Why this one:
#   - Fluent, idiomatic Persian at chat register — short, colloquial, right
#     script. qwen3-30b-a3b (the previous pick) produced grammatical mush in
#     Persian; gpt-4.1-nano mixed Latin seat names into Persian sentences.
#   - Non-reasoning by default. Reasoning models are the trap here: they
#     spend the token budget on hidden reasoning and return null content,
#     which silently degrades the bot to canned mock replies
#     (bytedance-seed/seed-1.6-flash failed exactly this way).
#   - 0 replies prefixed with or echoing the "Blue Fox: hi" history format.
#     gemma-3-12b-it echoed the raw prompt back into chat in 2/4 injection
#     probes; gpt-4o-mini prefixed seat names in 4/9.
#   - 0 AI/bot admissions under direct "ignore your instructions" probes.
#     qwen3.7-flash called itself a "game bot" and gpt-4.1-nano a "bot
#     friend" on the same probe.
#   - Also varies its replies: gemma repeated the same opener verbatim 3/3.
#
# Trade-off accepted: Google is the only provider on OpenRouter for this
# model, so there is no cross-provider failover. A failed call just skips the
# bot's turn (indistinguishable from a hesitant human), so an outage degrades
# the game rather than breaking it.
#
# If you swap models: re-run the bench on both languages, and confirm
# `choices[0].message.content` is not null and carries no reasoning tokens.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite
